    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Crash is the Human League’s fifth studio album, released in 1986 on Virgin Records and produced by Jimmy Jam and Terry Lewis. It marked a sharp stylistic shift from the band’s earlier synth-pop, leaning into polished Minneapolis-style electronic R&B and dance-pop, with sleek drum programming, glossy keyboards, and a more overtly soulful edge.\n\nThe album is best known for “Human,” a major international hit that gave the band a second U.S. number one single and helped re-establish them commercially after a difficult period. While some longtime listeners viewed the production as a departure from the group’s colder early sound, Crash is widely remembered as a successful, era-defining crossover that fused machine-driven pop with contemporary soul textures.",
